{"id":"04468c5f9b8242c0","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-central-simple.md","title":"Central Simple Algebra","display":"df-central-simple — Central Simple Algebra","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-central-simple","aliases":["58-df-central-simple"],"display":"df-central-simple — Central Simple Algebra","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-central-simple"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-central-simple</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-central-simple — Central Simple Algebra"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"10d54928fc77535a\" href=\"?note=10d54928fc77535a\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md\">../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,F\\in V\">\\(A,F\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S\\)</span> (canonical predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"10d54928fc77535a\" href=\"?note=10d54928fc77535a\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md\">../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CentralSimple}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{CentralSimple}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (compatibility predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}central\\text{-}simple} \\vdash \\mathrm{CentralSimple}_S(A,F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S(A,F)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}central\\text{-}simple} \\vdash \\mathrm{CentralSimple}_S(A,F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S(A,F)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom is a compatibility alias for the canonical definition, which also requires finite dimensionality, simplicity, and center exactly <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Tensor product of central simple algebras is again central simple.</li>\n<li>The Brauer group <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Br}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{Br}(F)\\)</span> classifies central simple algebras up to Brauer equivalence.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md","status":"resolved","id":"10d54928fc77535a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md","status":"resolved","id":"10d54928fc77535a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S$ (canonical predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-central-simple-algebra.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,F\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CentralSimple}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}central\\text{-}simple} \\vdash \\mathrm{CentralSimple}_S(A,F)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{CentralSimpleAlgebra}_S(A,F)","display":true},{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Br}(F)","display":false}],"bytes":1016,"backlinks":[{"id":"84da